WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
Scientific research is typically pictured
as a pure pursuit of truth and

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.240
societal benefit, a process driven by
objectivity and noble intentions.

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.680
But the process contains complex
vulnerabilities.

4
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.680
Hidden, systemic failures cascade through
a project, compromising the

5
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.740
outcomes, communities, and the researchers
themselves.

6
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.860
This brings us to the formal framework of
research risk management developed

7
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.640
under the Brie-Gret project with support
from the European Union.

8
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.580
Proactive architectural design embeds
ethical values into the research life

9
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.880
cycle long before regulatory deadlines
arrive.

10
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.900
This graphic illustrates the reality of
research risk as an iceberg operating

11
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.460
on two distinct levels of visibility.

12
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.320
Above the surface we see the highly
visible infractions.

13
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.800
These are the sharp, immediate crises that
typically trigger regulatory action

14
00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.600
and public scrutiny, overt data
fabrication sits at the very top,

15
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.400
a measurable symptom of a broken process.

16
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.520
To the left, data privacy violations
expose subjects to immediate harm and

17
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.160
legal penalties. On the right, intellectual
property conflicts over ownership

18
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.120
reliably trigger highly visible disputes.

19
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:19.880
But these visible peaks are supported by a
massive, submerged structure of

20
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.900
cultural and systemic failures.

21
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.400
Down here, subtle power imbalances within
research teams silently distort data

22
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.740
collection and compromise lab safety.

23
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.400
Exploitative or inequitable collaborations
extract value from vulnerable

24
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.040
partners, causing long-term damage to
community trust.

25
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.940
Anchoring the entire mass is institutional
complacency, the quiet acceptance

26
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:47.280
of poor practices that provides the
environment for all other risks to thrive.

27
00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:51.980
Attempting to police the visible symptoms
above the water is an exercise in

28
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.100
futility unless you dismantle the
submerged structural causes below it.
